s-module/articleshow/135197586.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197586.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbse-makes-ai-a-part-of-formal-teaching-ncert-develops-module/articleshow/135197586.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbse-makes-ai-a-part-of-formal-teaching-ncert-develops-module/articleshow/135197586.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T03:15:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Manash Pratim Gohain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197587,imgsize-182404.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[EC refuses to give details of SIR software, cites ‘trade secrets, IPR']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-refuses-to-give-details-of-sir-software-cites-trade-secrets-ipr/articleshow/135197575.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197575.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Election Commission of India declined to share the name of the software used for identifying electoral roll errors. The request for information was made under the Right to Information Act. A social activist from Telangana sought details about the software and algorithms used in the process. The Commission stated that no new software was developed for the exercise conducted.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-refuses-to-give-details-of-sir-software-cites-trade-secrets-ipr/articleshow/135197575.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ec-refuses-to-give-details-of-sir-software-cites-trade-secrets-ipr/articleshow/135197575.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T03:04:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197584,imgsize-98916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Former CJI D Y Chandrachud was more deferential to government than needed, says Justice Kaul]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/former-cji-d-y-chandrachud-was-more-deferential-to-government-than-needed-says-justice-kaul/articleshow/135197538.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197538.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Justice Sanjay Kishan Kaul has expressed concerns about how former Chief Justice D Y Chandrachud dealt with the government. He believes Chandrachud was too lenient during the process of judicial appointments, which raises worries about the independence of the judiciary. This could potentially undermine the separation between the courts and the government, according to Kaul.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/former-cji-d-y-chandrachud-was-more-deferential-to-government-than-needed-says-justice-kaul/articleshow/135197538.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/former-cji-d-y-chandrachud-was-more-deferential-to-government-than-needed-says-justice-kaul/articleshow/135197538.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T02:28:37+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197540,imgsize-235466.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[EPFO considers Rs 25,000cr war chest to stabilise interest payouts]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/epfo-considers-rs-25000cr-war-chest-to-stabilise-interest-payouts/articleshow/135197531.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197531.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation is exploring the establishment of a Rs 25,000-crore Interest Stabilisation Reserve. This reserve aims to protect members’ interest payouts from corporate bond defaults and other market fluctuations. A report suggested that the fund should be built via surplus ETF gains and will invest in government securities. Historical performance indicates that this reserve can effectively manage interest rate stability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/epfo-considers-rs-25000cr-war-chest-to-stabilise-interest-payouts/articleshow/135197531.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/epfo-considers-rs-25000cr-war-chest-to-stabilise-interest-payouts/articleshow/135197531.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T02:18:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Shiva Rajora</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197536,imgsize-48170.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[BJP calls protest over Kharge’s ‘baap’ remark]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-calls-protest-over-kharges-baap-remark/articleshow/135197490.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197490.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge's comment about Prime Minister Narendra Modi's father sparked widespread outrage among BJP members. Following the incident, the BJP announced nationwide protests against Kharge's remarks, labeling them indecent and offensive. Union home minister Amit Shah criticized Congress for personal attacks and blamed it on their electoral disappointments. Kharge also condemned the ongoing Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls, describing it as a threat to democracy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-calls-protest-over-kharges-baap-remark/articleshow/135197490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-calls-protest-over-kharges-baap-remark/articleshow/135197490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T01:52:12+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197501,imgsize-104164.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Give mayors real powers, ensure timely civic audits, urban body heads tell Centre]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-mayors-real-powers-ensure-timely-civic-audits-urban-body-heads-tell-centre/articleshow/135197022.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197022.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-mayors-real-powers-ensure-timely-civic-audits-urban-body-heads-tell-centre/articleshow/135197022.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-mayors-real-powers-ensure-timely-civic-audits-urban-body-heads-tell-centre/articleshow/135197022.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T00:33:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197099,imgsize-130504.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Delhi Police file FIR against opposition MPs over alleged trespassing at Jamia during student protest]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-police-file-fir-against-congress-3-mps-over-alleged-trespassing-at-jamia-during-student-protest/articleshow/135194757.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135194757.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Delhi Police has launched an FIR targeting Congress MPs who attended the student protests at Jamia Millia Islamia. The MPs are accused of entering the university without permission amid ongoing demands for reinstating the students' union. Protesters are also calling for a halt to disciplinary measures against students and improved campus facilities, while university officials draft guidelines for upcoming union elections, adding to the complexity of the situation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-police-file-fir-against-congress-3-mps-over-alleged-trespassing-at-jamia-during-student-protest/articleshow/135194757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/delhi-police-file-fir-against-congress-3-mps-over-alleged-trespassing-at-jamia-during-student-protest/articleshow/135194757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T22:11:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135194790,imgsize-203362.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Women founders are building India's social startups, their representation in nonprofits outpaces corporate leadership by a big margin, shows study]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/women-founders-are-building-indias-social-startups-their-representation-in-nonprofits-outpaces-corporate-leadership-by-a-big-margin-shows-study/articleshow/135194517.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135194517.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/women-founders-are-building-indias-social-startups-their-representation-in-nonprofits-outpaces-corporate-leadership-by-a-big-margin-shows-study/articleshow/135194517.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/women-founders-are-building-indias-social-startups-their-representation-in-nonprofits-outpaces-corporate-leadership-by-a-big-margin-shows-study/articleshow/135194517.cms